@startuml C4-Dynamic-Globe-Bootstrap
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false

title Dynamic — Globe bootstrap (mount → render loop → dispose)

actor "Browser User" as user
participant "Theme Page\n(React)" as page <<ui>>
participant "Globe\n(AggregateRoot)" as globe
participant "LandMap" as land
participant "FlyingLine" as flying
participant "GlobeRenderer" as renderer
participant "GlobePointer" as pointer
participant "WebGL Canvas" as canvas

user -> page: 1. Open /globe-light or /globe-dark
page -> globe: 2. Globe.create(container, canvas, config, scheme, theme)
globe -> land: 3. createLandDots(material, scene)
land --> globe: 4. materials[]
globe -> flying: 5. createMesh / createMarker (per DEFAULT_FLIGHT_ROUTES)
flying --> globe: 6. meshes
globe -> renderer: 7. startRenderLoop()
renderer -> canvas: 8. requestAnimationFrame render
globe -> pointer: 9. createInteraction(...)
pointer --> globe: 10. interaction + state
globe --> page: 11. GlobeContext
page --> user: 12. Interactive globe

note right of page
  On unmount: GlobeContext.dispose()
  stops rAF and removes listeners
end note

user -> page: 13. Leave route / unmount
page -> globe: 14. dispose()
globe -> renderer: 15. cancelAnimationFrame
globe -> pointer: 16. dispose listeners

@enduml
